Discover the running ZCode Desktop's Computer Use broker from the managed runtime

Purpose: paseo-plugin-zcode-provider (fork) enables Computer Use for Paseo
sessions. The standalone Server captures and strips
ZCODE_CUA_PERMISSION_BROKER_SOCKET before spawning the agent, and under
ZCODE_SERVICE_AUTHORITY_MODE=standalone-server it does not start its own
Helper. The agent therefore cannot see the Desktop Helper's named pipe. This
patch makes captureZCodeCuaBrokerCredentials recover the running Desktop
Helper's pipe when the env carries no complete credential pair. The Desktop
broker does not validate the authority nonce; the placeholder only has to match
the trusted shared node_repl server config.

Target: captureZCodeCuaBrokerCredentials in packages/shared/src/runtimeEnv.ts
(ZCode 3.16.2, 3c5b227649371507ddc4eb46ac5133afe6db1cab).

Remove when: ZCode provides an official way to attach a standalone Server to the
Desktop CUA broker, or the provider stops enabling Computer Use.

License: Apache-2.0, the license of the modified ZCode source.

Fork note: ADR 19 limits patches to hiding capabilities. This patch intentionally
enables a capability in this fork and requires a running ZCode Desktop.

